# Stack
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind CSS + Mantine 7.
- Light mode only. MantineProvider uses `forceColorScheme="light"`.
- Prototype only: no real API. All data comes from `src/mock/*.json` and local state.

# Source of truth
- Figma design system: file key `l3QZ1x8fDQEkEimzgwPInE` (iRM Design System).
- Figma screens: file key `UVuqMleArgUwsltkPjAtRX` (Designation Flow Hi-Fi).
- Before building any component or screen, call the Figma MCP (`get_design_context`, `get_variable_defs`, `get_screenshot`) for the given node. Never guess values.

# Layering (strict)
1. `src/styles/tokens.css`: all design tokens as CSS variables (generated from Figma variables). Only place hex values may appear.
2. `src/theme/mantine-theme.ts`: Mantine `createTheme` that reads the tokens (`var(--...)`). No hex values.
3. `tailwind.config.ts`: `theme.extend` maps colors, spacing, radius to the token variables. `corePlugins.preflight = false` (Mantine owns the reset).
4. `src/ds/*`: iRM components. Each one wraps a Mantine primitive and exposes props that match the Figma variant properties.
5. `src/features/designation/*`: screens. Build screens only from `src/ds/*`.

# Rules
- No hardcoded colours, spacing, radius or font sizes. Use token variables or Tailwind classes mapped to them.
- Use Tailwind for layout only (flex, grid, gap, padding, width). Use Mantine `styles`/`classNames` with token variables for component skins.
- Never use Mantine default colours (`blue.6` etc.) or the Mantine default `color` prop. Always go through the iRM wrapper.
- If a screen needs a component that is not in `src/ds`, stop and ask. Do not inline a one-off.
- Every status is a text label plus colour, never colour alone.
- Meaningful text uses `--color-text-body`. Muted text only for non-essential hints.
- Keyboard and focus: focus ring is `--color-focus-link`, 2px inside. Do not remove outlines.
- Client components: add `'use client'` to anything using Mantine hooks or state.
- Fonts: Inter and Lato via `next/font`.

