# Badge status mapping (always with text)
- Ready, Validated, Created -> `completed`
- Creating, Linking, Syncing, ID entered -> `in-progress`
- Queued, Needed, Draft, Awaiting TR approval, Awaiting final approval -> `pending`
- Name clash, Too long, Awaiting SAP, Open, Wildcard, Higher risk -> `warning`
- Error, Gap found, Analysis failed, Rejected -> `error`
- Auth objects: Standard = `light`, Maintained = `completed`, Changed = `dot`, Manual = `outline`, Inactive = `pending`, "SAP default" = `light`
- Published -> `completed`

# Domain rules for the prototype
- SAP role names max 30 characters. Business labels have no limit.
- Mock data is always 50+ (50 new roles, 20 existing roles, second page).
- Method (Option A or B) locks once creation starts (A) or once the requirement is sent (B).
- Name clash is fixed on Screen 8. Open org levels (KOKRS, WERKS) block Create.
- Footers always say why the primary action is disabled, with a Link to the problem.
- Sample data: Revenue Recognition `Z_SD_REVREC_CHG_1000`; plants 1000 Hamburg, 1010 Berlin, 2000 New York, 3000 Singapore, 4000 Shanghai. Mark invented names as sample data.

# Working style
- One screen or component per task. After building, run `next build` type check, then compare with `get_screenshot` of the Figma node and list differences.
- Report anything missing or ambiguous before improvising.

## Designation flow
For anything about screens, flow, statuses or business rules, read `docs/FLOW_GUIDE.md` first.
Reuse existing code in `src/ds/` (components) and `src/features/designation/` (screens).
Do not create new components if one exists in `src/ds/`.